# MIUI Camera branches its permission flow on ro.product.mod_device: when the
# value contains "_global" it asks Android for the camera permissions itself,
# otherwise it launches the HyperOS Security Center permissions dialog, which
# does not exist here. Stock puts ro.product.mod_device=songyuan in
# mi_ext/etc/build.prop - a partition this build has no equivalent of - and gets
# away with it because Security Center is present there.
#
# The device tree already carries patches/0001, which forces the same branch by
# clobbering the flag register in smali. Setting the property is the equivalent
# without touching the stock-signed APK; only the "_global" substring matters.
#
# It has to be set here rather than in a build.prop: Android 12+ does not take
# ro.product.* keys defined in a partition build.prop, so the copy that landed in
# /vendor/build.prop was silently ignored and the viewfinder stayed frozen.
on init
    setprop ro.product.mod_device songyuan_global

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    write /sys/class/xm_power/charger/charger_common/reverse_quick_charge 0

# Novatek visual display processor (the AI display enhancement chip).
#
# The stock init script starts hal_visdisplaysrv_default unconditionally as part
# of class hal and the service has no runtime knob of its own, so the Settings
# switch drives it from here instead: persist.sys.disp_enhance is written by the
# XiaomiParts display enhancement page and these triggers turn the HAL on or off.
# The property persists, so it is also replayed at boot when init loads the
# stored values.
on property:persist.sys.disp_enhance=1
    start hal_visdisplaysrv_default

on property:persist.sys.disp_enhance=0
    stop hal_visdisplaysrv_default
